---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Probe board information and self-test

Usage: pogo probe [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  info      Firmware version, protocol version, board, uptime, driven pins
  selftest  Check INA226 presence, pin release, and idle I2C buses
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>     Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"
      --probe <SELECTOR>      Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]
  -f, --format <FORMAT>       Output format [default: human] [env: POGO_FORMAT=] [possible values:
                              human, json, jsonl]
      --config <PATH>         Config file [env: POGO_CONFIG=]
      --timeout <DURATION>    Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m
      --wait-lock <DURATION>  Wait for a busy device instead of failing
      --dry-run               Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing
  -v, --verbose...            More logs on stderr (repeatable)
  -q, --quiet                 Errors only on stderr
      --no-color              Disable colors
